Theorem RL-17: OwnerBound is a dynamic upper bound

  Preconditions:
    - OwnershipObservationFacts preserves exact additional-credit,
      release, and sharing-observation identities.
    - Loop/global reachability and external retention are conservative signals.

  Soundness property:
    Forall additional-credit event sequence R:

      (P1) straight-line non-unique ownership yields OwnerBound.Bounded(|R|),
           whose capacity is |R| + 1 including the original owner.

      (P2) a local unique value without a widening signal yields Bounded(0).

      (P3) loop/global or externally retainable values yield Unbounded.

      (P4) loop/global precedence dominates local uniqueness.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive classification with the load-bearing row
    local_unique=true and loop_or_global=true -> Unbounded.

    Part (P1/P2/P3/P4) - owner-bound grid:
      local_unique_one_owner -> Bounded(0)
      three_additional_credits_four_owners -> Bounded(3)
      local_unique_loop_unbounded -> Unbounded
      external_credit_creation_unbounded -> Unbounded
      Coverage gate: 4 owner-bound cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl17_owner_bound;
        ownerBound and ownerCapacity classification)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-17 with dynamic OwnerBound capacity and loop/global or external-retention precedence over local uniqueness
